Sensitive parameters in CHEASE:

NSMOOTH: control whether the plasma boundary can be well contructed by 
         Fourier expansion.  =0 is good.

SOLPDA: very important to control the q-profile, =0.5 is better than
        =0.4

B0EXP, R0EXP: should be set up in the NAMELIST in order to get correct 
              current in the output.

NCSCAL=4: no value of q at one point is needed to be specified,
          important for constructing equilibrium from EQDSK

Boundary shape (R,Z): should be normalized such that R0=1
 
psi>0:  consider the sign of P' and TT'

When change COMMON blocks, don't forget to change block size in COMDIM

Good parameter set for CHEASE:
   NS=NT=60, NCHI=256, MSMAX=60, shape is good, q is bad at center
   NS=NT=46, NCHI=92,  MSMAX=22, both shape and q are good
     
Very important!: always choose NCHI as even number

In order to better resolve magnetic axis, use the following packing for 
the sigma-mesh:
   NMESHC=1, NPOIDC=1, SOLPDC=0.8, CPLACE=0.0,CWIDTH=0.020,
